## Why This Is Asked
New angle: per-block setup cost while selecting up to k blocks, non-overlapping; tests ability to derive a compact DP with prefix sums and a best-so-far trick; includes reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays with a per-block cost
- Prefix sums to compute block values quickly
- Best-so-far technique to achieve O(nk) time
- Reconstruction pointers for endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKBlocksWithCost(A, k, cost) {
  const n = A.length;
  const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) P[i] = P[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => new Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  const bestVal = new Array(k+1).fill(NEG);
  bestVal[0] = 0; // dp[0][0] - P[0]

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const candidate = P[i] - cost + bestVal[t-1];
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], candidate);
    }
    // update bestVal for next i
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const val = dp[i][t-1] - P[i];
      if (val > bestVal[t]) bestVal[t] = val;
    }
  }
  return { dp, P };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests dynamic programming with a non-adjacency constraint and explicit reconstruction of the deletion indices.

## Key Concepts
- DP with two states per index to enforce non-adjacency
- Exact deletions constraint (k) and reconstruction
- O(nk) time and O(nk) space (can optimize to O(k) with rolling arrays)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumAfterDeletions(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const keep = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const del = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  keep[0][0] = A[0];
  if (k >= 1) del[0][1] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      keep[i][t] = Math.max(keep[i-1][t], del[i-1][t]);
      if (keep[i][t] > NEG/2) keep[i][t] += A[i];
      if (t > 0) del[i][t] = keep[i-1][t-1];
    }
  }
  const end = Math.max(keep[n-1][k], del[n-1][k]);
  // Backtracking to collect deleted indices would be added here
  return {maxSum: end, deletedIndices: []};
}
```

